      "author": "Kate Cherven",
      "author_location": null,
      "trip_type": null,
      "title": null,
      "text": "Salt+Scoria is a wonderful addition to the food options in Medora. Nestled in the TR Library the space feels like a warm and soothing space. It was wonderful to see a Native American Restaurant supporting local farmers and indigenous communities. This spot reminded me of Off The Rez cafe in the Burke Museum at the University of Washington in Seattle. I got the smoked chicken kebab salad and the sea salt chocolate chip cookies with an iced oat milk latte. You could smell the wood smoke off the chicken when it arrived, the flavor reminded me of other BBQ spots in MT, and the greens were dressed perfectly. I found it hard to find a refreshing quick meal in Medora and this hit the spot. And the cookies were deliciously gooey and decedent. Best of all, the staff are so lovely and curious and open to feedback on the food since they just opened. 10/10 would recommend, even if you've already done the museum you should sit at the cafe and enjoy the food and views.",
